WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:03.938 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:06.066 --> 01:07.150
EMERGENCY ROOM

01:17.202 --> 01:18.578
[middle-aged Ae-sun whimpers]

01:21.664 --> 01:23.416
So, actually,

01:24.417 --> 01:26.461
I lived in that room a few years ago.

01:27.504 --> 01:30.799
There was always a draft because
the windows were so bent out of shape.

01:30.882 --> 01:32.842
I suppose that's what saved her today.

01:35.637 --> 01:37.806
Oh God. What if I hadn't made it?

01:38.723 --> 01:40.266
What if I'd missed the flight?

01:40.975 --> 01:44.020
I don't know why,
but I just knew I had to come.

01:45.271 --> 01:47.148
You saved her life, ma'am, you did.

01:47.649 --> 01:48.608
No. No.

01:49.317 --> 01:51.528
Geum-myeong's the one who saved my life.

01:53.488 --> 01:56.241
By staying alive, she saved my life.

01:56.825 --> 01:58.618
She's much kinder than I am.

01:59.786 --> 02:01.871
I really can't take this anymore.

02:03.581 --> 02:04.666
I really can't.

02:10.922 --> 02:12.632
You have to stay healthy

02:12.715 --> 02:15.093
'cause Geum-myeong still needs you. Here.

02:15.718 --> 02:16.761
[middle-aged Ae-sun] Oh my.

02:18.138 --> 02:22.600
Uh, are you the landlord's son-in-law?

02:23.309 --> 02:24.936
Well, uh…

02:30.275 --> 02:31.192
[pants]

02:31.818 --> 02:32.652
That's

02:33.236 --> 02:35.196
Park Geum-myeong's son, no?

02:35.280 --> 02:36.156
[Chung-seob] Huh?

02:37.532 --> 02:38.533
Park Geum-myeong's son?

02:39.242 --> 02:40.076
Huh?

02:40.910 --> 02:44.122
I mean, I never knew who his dad was.

02:44.205 --> 02:46.207
[jaunty music playing]

02:56.885 --> 02:57.927
[sighs] Gimme.

03:00.096 --> 03:01.097
[Geum-myeong] What?

03:07.312 --> 03:08.646
[Yeong-beom] You're freezing.

03:11.941 --> 03:13.735
[Ae-sun] It's not like you are nobility.

03:15.236 --> 03:17.280
Why won't you let me take care of you?

03:17.363 --> 03:18.907
Hush now, okay?

03:19.407 --> 03:21.326
Let's talk about this later.

03:21.409 --> 03:22.869
We should get married now.

03:22.952 --> 03:24.871
Let's just go and get it over with.

03:25.496 --> 03:26.998
[Geum-myeong] Quiet! My mom's here.

03:27.624 --> 03:28.583
[Yeong-beom sighs]

03:31.336 --> 03:34.297
Tell them to go play house somewhere else.

03:34.380 --> 03:36.257
Goodness, she's all grown up.

03:38.927 --> 03:39.886
[nurse] Excuse me.

03:40.553 --> 03:41.888
Have you filled this out yet?

03:42.847 --> 03:44.307
Oh, right.

03:46.643 --> 03:49.145
[Yeong-beom] If you didn't want it,
why did you take the ring?

03:49.229 --> 03:51.898
With the ring,
it's a done deal. A done deal!

03:53.650 --> 03:56.694
Don't go. Marry me. Here's a ring.
You take the ring, and it's a done deal.

03:56.778 --> 03:57.862
[sighs]

03:58.404 --> 04:01.699
How did she find a boy
just like her father?

04:01.783 --> 04:03.284
[Yeong-beom] I told you to move.

04:03.368 --> 04:06.204
-Enough, please.
-I told you to move out of there.

04:06.287 --> 04:08.248
Have you ever been poisoned before?

04:08.331 --> 04:11.209
The doctor said being nagged at
will give me more headaches.

04:11.292 --> 04:13.753
But why did you have to be
poisoned in the first place?

04:14.379 --> 04:18.466
Just marry me and move in with us.
I mean, we even have a water heater.

04:18.549 --> 04:20.885
[Geum-myeong] You're proposing to me
with a water heater?

04:20.969 --> 04:22.762
What happened to the diamond ring?

04:22.845 --> 04:26.391
Jeez, I guess they have no shame,
talking on and on.

04:26.474 --> 04:28.935
[Yeong-beom] I'm not asking
for anything unreasonable.

04:29.018 --> 04:30.937
They don't fix street lights
in that neighborhood.

04:31.020 --> 04:33.648
I hate that you have to climb
that hill by yourself.

04:34.274 --> 04:36.943
I hate that you can see
your own breath in that room.

04:37.026 --> 04:40.947
I hate that you can't sleep because
you have to sell late-night movie tickets.

04:41.030 --> 04:43.908
I hate that you can't make phone calls
because of your landlord.

04:43.992 --> 04:44.867
I hate it all.

04:44.951 --> 04:47.537
Why do you have to put up with it?
No one else does.

04:47.620 --> 04:49.247
Who wants to live like that?

04:49.330 --> 04:50.540
Nobody!

04:53.209 --> 04:54.752
-Don't you watch the news?
-[sighs]

04:55.253 --> 04:58.548
It happens in the blink of an eye.
You can die in an instant.

04:58.631 --> 05:01.759
What if you died from carbon monoxide
when you were alone? Huh?

05:02.593 --> 05:04.846
What if something happens and you die?

05:04.929 --> 05:06.806
Yeah, but I didn't die.

05:08.391 --> 05:09.809
[Yeong-beom sobs]

05:10.393 --> 05:12.520
-I couldn't take it!
-[Geum-myeong] Come on.

05:13.229 --> 05:14.564
What's wrong?

05:14.647 --> 05:17.358
I thought boys stopped crying
after basic training.

05:18.443 --> 05:20.528
Seriously, you're an officer.

05:20.611 --> 05:23.448
If you die, I'll die too.

05:23.531 --> 05:25.783
That's all I could think in the taxi here.

05:25.867 --> 05:26.784
Hey,

05:27.410 --> 05:29.162
no matter what, life goes on.

05:29.662 --> 05:31.080
So if I died, you'd move on?

05:31.581 --> 05:33.958
I mean, eventually.

05:34.042 --> 05:35.501
Yeah, I would.

05:41.507 --> 05:42.383
Stop smiling.

05:42.967 --> 05:43.843
Hmm?

05:44.552 --> 05:45.720
[Geum-myeong chuckles]

05:45.803 --> 05:47.263
Oh, you're too cute.

05:47.889 --> 05:49.640
It's so annoying.

05:49.724 --> 05:50.683
[sobs]

05:50.767 --> 05:53.811
It wasn't that bad.
It was just a little gas.

05:53.895 --> 05:56.606
Besides, you know I have tiny nostrils.

05:56.689 --> 05:59.150
I couldn't inhale that much,
even if I wanted to.

06:01.986 --> 06:02.945
[sniffles]

06:04.072 --> 06:05.198
Geum-myeong,

06:05.948 --> 06:07.492
please don't ever be alone.

06:08.618 --> 06:09.619
Please?

06:10.495 --> 06:11.954
I'm the one you're marrying.

06:12.663 --> 06:14.624
It's not like you'd be marrying my mom.

06:16.584 --> 06:19.629
I'll do whatever it takes
for my family to give us their blessing.

06:20.129 --> 06:22.673
Ae-sun will live with me.
She won't be living with my grandmother.

06:23.424 --> 06:25.510
I'll make sure
she won't lay a hand on her.

06:25.593 --> 06:28.179
I'll make sure my mom
takes it easy on you.

06:28.763 --> 06:31.682
She has her opinions, but you just
have to butter her up a little.

06:31.766 --> 06:34.936
She doesn't like me.
I don't really like her either.

06:35.019 --> 06:36.270
[gentle piano music playing]

06:36.354 --> 06:39.357
Deep down, my mom is a nice person.

06:39.440 --> 06:42.610
But if she is so nice,
why was she so rude at our family dinner?

06:47.156 --> 06:49.325
-What did she say to you?
-Oh my God.

06:50.034 --> 06:51.494
You scared me.

06:51.577 --> 06:53.162
-Hello there, Mrs. Oh.
-That's how it is?

06:53.246 --> 06:55.289
Your mother doesn't approve
of my daughter. That true?

06:56.207 --> 06:58.876
No, Mom. That's not what we meant.

06:58.960 --> 07:01.045
Why not? Why?

07:01.671 --> 07:02.797
[Geum-myeong sighs]

07:11.013 --> 07:13.015
[music playing on TV]

07:16.853 --> 07:19.188
[woman 5] I can't believe my own eyes.

07:21.941 --> 07:23.901
Are you really Sang-gil's daughter?

07:24.402 --> 07:25.611
Mm-hmm.

07:26.446 --> 07:28.030
Ooh. This is hilarious.

07:28.614 --> 07:30.116
Why is it funny who her dad is?

07:30.199 --> 07:31.868
I think he'd be proud, is all.

07:31.951 --> 07:33.953
She's living out his dream.

07:34.036 --> 07:36.414
Cut the bullcrap.
They don't need to hear it.

07:36.497 --> 07:38.416
Many years ago,
your mother and your father

07:38.499 --> 07:40.209
sat across from each other in those seats.

07:40.293 --> 07:43.671
-Hey.
-This was a café. They met for coffee.

07:43.754 --> 07:45.882
-Hey.
-[Gyeong-ja] They were on a blind date.

07:46.591 --> 07:48.468
You two could've been siblings.

07:49.093 --> 07:51.220
Watch it. Ae-sun is gonna kill you.

07:52.138 --> 07:54.098
[Gyeong-ja] You're just like
Romeo and Juliet.

07:54.932 --> 07:56.350
Mm. Bit uglier though.

07:56.434 --> 07:57.602
[chuckles]

07:57.685 --> 07:58.519
[kettle whistling]

07:58.603 --> 08:00.646
[Geum-myeong]
Will their first great love last,

08:01.272 --> 08:04.692
or will it only be
a heartbreaking memory of young love?

08:07.695 --> 08:11.365
At the time, they were completely
caught up in their emotions

08:11.449 --> 08:12.617
without holding back.

08:14.118 --> 08:16.370
What does your mother not like
about my daughter? Tell me.

08:16.454 --> 08:18.039
No, ma'am, I didn't mean…

08:18.748 --> 08:21.375
As her guardian,
we need you to sign this form.

08:23.586 --> 08:25.463
-[Chung-seob] Me?
-[nurse] Of course, who else?

08:25.546 --> 08:27.465
You are her guardian. Aren't you?

08:27.548 --> 08:28.633
Oh, I'm not--

08:28.716 --> 08:32.720
But you brought her in. I saw you.
You ran here with her on your back.

08:32.803 --> 08:33.888
Who is he?

08:35.473 --> 08:36.390
[sighs]

08:37.725 --> 08:39.185
[Yeong-beom] Why is he your guardian?

08:39.268 --> 08:41.729
You know what? I don't like her son.

08:45.316 --> 08:46.817
I'm talking about you.

08:47.985 --> 08:50.947
Just tell me if they dated.
Give me a simple yes or no.

08:51.030 --> 08:53.783
Are you just
making stuff up again or what?

08:53.866 --> 08:56.953
Hey, if I tell you,
will you rat me out to your dad?

08:57.036 --> 08:58.788
You can't fool me.
Remember when I was little,

08:58.871 --> 09:00.957
you convinced me
you had a tiger at your house?

09:01.457 --> 09:03.000
[Gyeong-ja] Okay, just forget it.

09:03.501 --> 09:07.213
Good, drop it. There are some things
better off left in the past.

09:09.632 --> 09:11.092
[Gyeong-ja] They never dated.

09:14.720 --> 09:16.806
However, they almost got married.

09:16.889 --> 09:18.182
[chuckles]

09:18.266 --> 09:20.268
[jaunty music playing]

09:29.026 --> 09:30.653
[music fades]

09:43.124 --> 09:44.709
You think that's funny?

09:44.792 --> 09:47.795
[laughter]

09:47.878 --> 09:49.630
Ah. A little bit.

09:55.177 --> 09:56.971
THREE AUNTIES'
FRESHLY PICKED BY HAENYEO

10:05.146 --> 10:07.148
[gentle piano music playing]

10:10.192 --> 10:11.485
[sighs]

10:15.531 --> 10:17.533
What in God's name
is that thing on your head?

10:17.617 --> 10:19.035
Are you about to plow a field?

10:19.118 --> 10:20.161
Hey, Dad,

10:21.537 --> 10:22.538
are you happy?

10:22.622 --> 10:24.832
Ah, you can't really think
that makes you look good.

10:25.541 --> 10:28.336
Just shave your head.
I'll pay you 50,000 won.

10:28.419 --> 10:29.920
[razor whirring]

10:30.004 --> 10:32.006
[rock music playing]

10:34.216 --> 10:35.968
[music continues in headphones]

10:40.640 --> 10:41.641
THIS IS NOT TRASH

10:41.724 --> 10:44.185
THIS IS MY PRIDE I'VE THROWN AWAY FOR YOU

10:44.268 --> 10:45.478
COME BACK TO ME, YEM

10:47.271 --> 10:50.900
HYEON-SUK LOVES YOU FOEVER

10:50.983 --> 10:53.110
26 MONTHS OR 26 YEARS
I PROMISE I WILL WAIT

10:53.194 --> 10:54.320
[sobs]

11:03.287 --> 11:05.665
Do people still get beat up
in the military?

11:05.748 --> 11:07.249
I never taught you how to handle that.

11:07.333 --> 11:09.502
Why did you insist on coming
if you were gonna cry?

11:09.585 --> 11:10.586
Jeez, seriously.

11:11.671 --> 11:12.505
[Eun-myeong sighs]

11:12.588 --> 11:15.299
[sobs] You should've gone to college.
I knew you should.

11:15.383 --> 11:16.634
[radio] With the implementation

11:16.717 --> 11:19.220
of the College Scholastic Ability Test
this year,

11:19.303 --> 11:22.181
many students are experiencing
quite a lot of confusion.

11:22.807 --> 11:25.976
While the Academic Ability Exam
was based on memorization,

11:26.060 --> 11:28.646
this new test is geared
toward comprehensive reasoning…

11:28.729 --> 11:31.273
[middle-aged Ae-sun] They expect kids
to run before they can even walk.

11:31.357 --> 11:34.944
If they keep changing the exams,
how can the slower kids go to college?

11:35.986 --> 11:36.904
[sobs]

11:36.987 --> 11:38.489
[Geum-myeong] He joined the army?

11:38.572 --> 11:39.782
[woman] Last-minute decision.

11:40.324 --> 11:43.786
He hasn't done his military service yet?

11:44.370 --> 11:46.956
I know he looks old enough
to have fought in the war,

11:47.456 --> 11:49.417
but our Picasso is only 28.

11:51.001 --> 11:53.337
He said soju and popcorn are for the boss.

11:53.421 --> 11:55.381
Everything else is up for grabs.

11:56.215 --> 11:57.508
Popcorn for me?

11:58.134 --> 12:00.302
How can he leave without saying goodbye?

12:00.386 --> 12:01.762
Why didn't he tell us?

12:01.846 --> 12:04.640
I can't eat all of this on my own.
It's too much.

12:04.724 --> 12:06.559
We worked together for years.

12:06.642 --> 12:09.895
Are you quitting too?
I guess you won't be seeing him again.

12:09.979 --> 12:12.606
We might run into each other… again.

12:12.690 --> 12:13.816
No, you won't.

12:13.899 --> 12:16.736
You won't see him again in this life.
Maybe the next.

12:16.819 --> 12:20.448
The stars have to align for you
to meet someone once in a lifetime.

12:21.449 --> 12:22.950
If you let them pass you by.

12:23.451 --> 12:25.578
I'm afraid that's all she wrote.

12:37.631 --> 12:38.674
[sighs]

12:39.508 --> 12:41.927
Apparently, he carried me just like that.

12:42.720 --> 12:45.347
NEVER LET YOUR GUARD DOWN
NEVER LET THEM OUT OF YOUR SIGHT

12:45.431 --> 12:47.558
AND NEVER FALL IN LOVE
THE BODYGUARD

12:49.101 --> 12:51.312
Seoul boys are heartless after all.

12:56.358 --> 12:58.360
[intriguing music playing]

13:03.657 --> 13:04.617
[Geum-myeong] That year,

13:04.700 --> 13:07.620
everything about my life
seemed to be shifting.

13:19.465 --> 13:25.304
[man on TV] And the grand prize winner
of the 1993 KBS Korean Music Awards is…

13:25.387 --> 13:26.972
[drum roll]

13:29.016 --> 13:30.935
…Kim Soo-hee for "Sad Love"!

13:31.018 --> 13:32.561
[cheering]

13:32.645 --> 13:35.189
[Geum-myeong]
Kim Soo-hee defeated Seo Taiji.

13:35.689 --> 13:38.943
The winds of fall
overcame the passions of spring.

13:39.026 --> 13:43.322
[man on TV] The year 1993, a year filled
with all kinds of ups and downs,

13:43.405 --> 13:44.907
is finally coming to a close.

13:45.491 --> 13:49.411
[Geum-myeong] Fighting the wind
that rages in our hearts is a losing game.

13:49.495 --> 13:51.872
So, have I changed a lot?

13:51.956 --> 13:53.958
[romantic pop music playing]

13:58.546 --> 14:01.382
The wind always blows in the fall.

14:01.465 --> 14:02.800
[music fades]

14:06.428 --> 14:08.430
[intriguing music playing]

14:12.184 --> 14:14.353
But it also blows in the spring.

14:15.437 --> 14:18.691
Oh jeez.
How does he expect me to sell this thing?

14:19.859 --> 14:21.402
Whatever the season,

14:21.485 --> 14:23.153
it blows and blows.

14:25.906 --> 14:27.324
I'd like to think that.

14:27.908 --> 14:28.951
I'd like to.

14:29.535 --> 14:32.079
[Geum-myeong] Our hearts
never cease to be moved.

14:38.043 --> 14:39.587
[Geum-myeong] "I, a poor man,

14:40.087 --> 14:43.507
love the beautiful Natasha dearly."

14:43.591 --> 14:46.176
"So tonight, the snow falls heavily."

14:46.719 --> 14:49.930
Oh, so you saw that too. [sighs]

14:50.014 --> 14:52.808
I guess you like that one especially.

14:54.059 --> 14:55.477
Well, I just…

14:56.145 --> 14:58.022
So you're a sentimental one.

15:03.527 --> 15:04.820
[Chung-seob] I suppose

15:05.446 --> 15:09.074
in poetry, poverty can seem dignified.

15:09.825 --> 15:12.036
There's nothing cool about
not having money,

15:13.287 --> 15:14.872
but poetry gives it beauty.

15:16.999 --> 15:17.917
Well,

15:19.376 --> 15:20.544
you're a painter.

15:22.129 --> 15:23.881
I couldn't paint to save my life.

15:27.551 --> 15:29.511
You use that talent to make money.

15:30.554 --> 15:32.056
Not everyone can do that.

15:34.099 --> 15:35.559
So, Mr. Toto,

15:35.643 --> 15:37.978
I'm afraid you're not so poor after all.

15:38.062 --> 15:39.480
And if I may be so blunt,

15:39.563 --> 15:42.733
your Natasha
isn't exactly beautiful either.

15:43.776 --> 15:45.986
Don't let her make you feel small.

15:47.529 --> 15:48.489
I mean,

15:48.989 --> 15:52.242
I don't know if anything I'm saying
will help you get over her.

15:54.411 --> 15:55.621
But your Natasha

15:56.246 --> 15:58.415
is a bit of a donkey
without her makeup on.

16:02.711 --> 16:03.754
Um…

16:06.298 --> 16:07.800
My mom was curious.

16:07.883 --> 16:10.928
Were you planning
to take any grad-school exams?

16:15.391 --> 16:16.934
She wants to give you books for it.

16:18.852 --> 16:20.854
[feel-good music playing]

16:31.490 --> 16:33.492
[distant siren wailing]

16:35.911 --> 16:39.373
[Geum-myeong] If you keep saying,
"I feel sorry for myself, my life sucks,"

16:39.456 --> 16:40.791
your life will suck.

16:41.834 --> 16:44.253
If you don't think you're worth 100 won,

16:44.336 --> 16:46.463
who's gonna think you're worth 1,000?

16:46.547 --> 16:50.175
So instead of
pitying yourself all the time,

16:50.259 --> 16:53.303
try to find the courage
to talk yourself up instead.

16:54.346 --> 16:56.473
You kinda look like
Master Roshi right now.

16:56.557 --> 16:58.350
[chuckles] Do you read Dragon Ball?

16:58.434 --> 17:01.729
Look, just be glad you're not my family.

17:01.812 --> 17:03.355
'Cause if you were my little brother…

17:04.314 --> 17:05.315
Pow.

17:05.858 --> 17:07.317
I'd beat some sense into you.

17:07.401 --> 17:08.819
[laughs]

17:09.903 --> 17:11.697
So you do know how to laugh.

17:12.740 --> 17:14.825
Wow. I didn't know I could.

17:25.377 --> 17:26.670
[music fades]

17:27.588 --> 17:28.630
So that's the tree?

17:35.471 --> 17:37.014
The biggest Christmas tree in Korea.

17:38.557 --> 17:39.558
Ah.

17:40.309 --> 17:42.978
I got this place
because of the hilltop view.

17:43.062 --> 17:46.398
If we go all the way up, we'll see
the biggest Christmas tree in Korea.

17:47.274 --> 17:48.108
Wow.

17:49.777 --> 17:53.572
I think we've seen each other in the most
embarrassing situations of our lives.

17:56.408 --> 17:57.659
I think you're like

17:58.786 --> 18:00.120
that Christmas tree over there.

18:02.498 --> 18:05.918
Trees do their job by just standing still
no matter where they are.

18:07.920 --> 18:08.921
Yeah, how so?

18:10.214 --> 18:11.090
Oh, you know.

18:11.882 --> 18:13.509
Wherever a Christmas tree is,

18:13.592 --> 18:16.303
if it's in an apartment
or a lonely corner store,

18:18.097 --> 18:20.099
it always shines bright, no matter what,

18:21.350 --> 18:22.601
and takes your breath away.

18:26.605 --> 18:28.774
I thought I should say that
on a day like today.

18:29.650 --> 18:30.651
It's like you said,

18:31.485 --> 18:33.112
I'm talking… talking people up.

18:41.912 --> 18:44.957
Hang on. Are you going away or something?

18:46.041 --> 18:48.043
[pop ballad playing]

18:52.631 --> 18:54.633
-[traffic noise]
-[car horns honking]

18:59.638 --> 19:02.141
MY LOVE BY MY SIDE

19:09.398 --> 19:12.609
MY LOVE BY MY SIDE
DAVICHI

19:18.490 --> 19:20.742
[siren wailing]

19:21.827 --> 19:25.706
[automated voice] Student passenger.
This stop is Neung-dong Intersection.

19:26.290 --> 19:28.041
Neung-dong Intersection.

19:28.542 --> 19:29.835
[pop music playing]

19:29.918 --> 19:33.172
[bus driver] Ma'am,
this is Neung-dong Intersection.

19:33.255 --> 19:34.423
This is your stop.

19:39.386 --> 19:41.388
[indistinct chattering]

19:56.445 --> 19:59.740
[Geum-myeong] There was a time
when everyone held their heads up.

20:04.870 --> 20:07.831
A time when people
were open about their feelings.

20:07.915 --> 20:08.999
KIM HYUN-SIK BEST HITS

20:09.082 --> 20:13.712
A time when we looked at each other
instead of our cell phones.

20:13.795 --> 20:15.422
[both laugh]

20:18.425 --> 20:19.509
Like it?

20:19.593 --> 20:20.677
I do.

20:20.761 --> 20:22.221
When did you record this?

20:23.138 --> 20:25.140
You said you like
Kim Hyun-sik more than me.

20:25.224 --> 20:26.808
I was joking.

20:38.237 --> 20:39.238
Tough day at work?

20:39.947 --> 20:41.031
It must not be fun.

20:43.242 --> 20:45.244
Nobody goes to work for fun.

20:45.869 --> 20:47.329
Everyone needs a check.

20:49.081 --> 20:51.333
Are you taking the bar for fun? [chuckles]

20:51.959 --> 20:53.043
[Yeong-beom] Even so,

20:53.877 --> 20:55.504
was this what you wanted to do?

20:56.505 --> 20:59.258
Hmm? Was it your dream
to work in an office?

21:00.801 --> 21:02.135
Mm…

21:03.220 --> 21:05.722
I just wanted to be free.

21:08.600 --> 21:09.601
Always have.

21:11.436 --> 21:13.855
Claiming independence as an individual

21:15.107 --> 21:17.818
is actually
a pretty impressive accomplishment.

21:19.945 --> 21:22.906
[Geum-myeong] But we never really
claimed independence.

21:22.990 --> 21:26.451
College, graduation,
introducing our families.

21:27.369 --> 21:30.831
Our parents were involved
in every aspect of our lives.

21:32.374 --> 21:34.126
Okay, that's it. We're leaving.

21:36.378 --> 21:37.296
They're almost here.

21:38.088 --> 21:40.132
The traffic is really bad in Seoul.

21:40.215 --> 21:42.509
They know we took a flight to get here,
don't they?

21:43.093 --> 21:45.929
[sighs] He should've left
a little bit earlier.

21:46.430 --> 21:48.348
How bad could the traffic be?

21:51.310 --> 21:54.062
Geum-myeong,
why are you being so anxious, dear?

21:54.646 --> 21:56.273
You always tell me to relax.

21:56.356 --> 21:57.941
You know what? Forget it.

21:58.734 --> 22:00.819
Don't be like that. Don't start.

22:00.902 --> 22:02.237
We should call it off.

22:10.037 --> 22:12.039
Oh, I'm sorry we're late.

22:12.122 --> 22:13.957
We hit traffic just as
we were getting close.

22:14.041 --> 22:15.000
[Geum-myeong] Oh, hello.

22:19.254 --> 22:20.756
[chuckles nervously]

22:20.839 --> 22:22.924
The traffic must've been awful.

22:23.008 --> 22:25.594
I hope none of you got carsick
on the way here.

22:26.261 --> 22:28.555
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
Geum-myeong was overly polite that day.

22:28.638 --> 22:29.723
We're very late.

22:29.806 --> 22:32.601
Oh, that's okay. It's all right.

22:33.226 --> 22:37.773
[Geum-myeong] My mom told a woman
who never once apologized, "It's okay."

22:38.815 --> 22:40.859
That was the dynamic in the room.

22:41.568 --> 22:44.488
We've met before. I'm Park Geum-myeong.

22:48.950 --> 22:51.078
[Geum-myeong] That day,
for the first time,

22:51.161 --> 22:54.498
I saw how my dad hides his callouses
when he shakes your hand.

22:54.581 --> 22:56.166
I'm Geum-myeong's father,

22:56.875 --> 22:58.168
Yang Gwan-sik.

23:01.171 --> 23:02.422
[Park Geum-myeong laughs]

23:02.506 --> 23:04.966
Eventually, the parents let the kids
have their way.

23:05.050 --> 23:06.718
I knew my wife would come around.

23:07.469 --> 23:09.554
If he wants to get married,
let's get things moving.

23:09.638 --> 23:12.432
Dating a girl for too long isn't
very polite on the man's part, is it?

23:12.516 --> 23:14.267
Think of the time she loses.

23:14.351 --> 23:16.478
Well, Yeong-beom is in no hurry.

23:16.561 --> 23:18.939
-[Park Geum-myeong laughs] Listen.
-Uh, Father?

23:19.022 --> 23:20.190
Thanks.

23:20.816 --> 23:22.651
I've been thinking. When they're married,

23:22.734 --> 23:25.487
they should really start
calling each other "honey."

23:25.570 --> 23:27.697
It'd be a bit weird
to hear my son calling his wife

23:27.781 --> 23:31.368
"Geum-myeong" all the time
since that's my name too. [laughs]

23:31.451 --> 23:33.954
It would be much better
if she had a different name.

23:34.538 --> 23:36.039
[Park Geum-myeong laughs]

23:38.500 --> 23:39.459
Help yourselves.

23:43.004 --> 23:45.924
[middle-aged Ae-sun] It's my fault.
I'm the one who taught her that.

23:51.346 --> 23:53.640
She's only doing what she saw growing up.

23:59.521 --> 24:00.522
Let's eat.

24:01.648 --> 24:02.607
Let's eat.

24:04.943 --> 24:06.278
Aren't you bringing out sungnyung?

24:08.697 --> 24:10.323
[middle-aged Ae-sun] My precious child.

24:11.116 --> 24:13.201
I should have shown her a better way.

24:13.785 --> 24:15.787
[Park Geum-myeong]
Here, have some steamed fish.

24:15.871 --> 24:18.248
[middle-aged Ae-sun] It broke my heart
to see that my daughter

24:18.331 --> 24:19.708
had turned out exactly like me.

24:19.791 --> 24:21.793
[Park Geum-myeong laughs]

24:24.880 --> 24:25.881
Mmm.

24:28.133 --> 24:31.386
[middle-aged Gwan-sik] We have a few dates
in mind for the wedding in Jeju.

24:32.012 --> 24:33.263
Did you not tell them?

24:36.558 --> 24:38.143
Why are you looking at him?

24:38.226 --> 24:40.479
Uh, Mom, I thought I told you--

24:40.562 --> 24:43.648
I'm afraid
having two weddings is unacceptable.

24:43.732 --> 24:45.400
We'd be a laughing stock.

24:45.484 --> 24:48.695
I can't have my son being paraded
down there like a show monkey.

24:49.821 --> 24:52.699
I understand
that the island has its own customs,

24:52.782 --> 24:55.952
but Geum-myeong will be
a part of our family now, not yours.

24:56.036 --> 24:58.288
I think her new family takes priority,
don't you?

25:06.713 --> 25:09.174
So in any case,
we should choose one place.

25:09.257 --> 25:12.636
Would you like to have it in Jeju?
We're willing to give up Seoul.

25:13.178 --> 25:15.847
No, uh, we should have it in Seoul.

25:17.098 --> 25:20.018
You'd be free from household chores
from now on. Congrats.

25:20.852 --> 25:24.481
[scoffs] I doubt it.
Look at how she ladled your soup.

25:25.065 --> 25:28.026
We have our work cut out for us, don't we?

25:30.403 --> 25:34.157
I'm not sure she can handle managing
our household when she knows so little.

25:34.699 --> 25:35.700
Well,

25:36.701 --> 25:38.161
that might be a bit much.

25:38.870 --> 25:40.205
She still has her job, after all.

25:40.288 --> 25:42.624
Yes, it would.
Which is why she'll stop working.

25:43.875 --> 25:44.876
Won't you?

25:45.794 --> 25:47.921
Mother, can we talk about this some--

25:48.004 --> 25:49.506
I wasn't speaking to you, son.

25:50.674 --> 25:53.260
Oh! I haven't tried the sungnyung.

25:53.802 --> 25:54.636
I…

25:55.178 --> 25:56.263
Oh, sure.

26:01.184 --> 26:04.145
I hope you know how to ladle
sungnyung at least.

26:06.439 --> 26:09.401
Most eldest daughters
do housework quite well.

26:09.484 --> 26:10.860
Geum-myeong is a bit different.

26:11.695 --> 26:12.529
It's strange.

26:12.612 --> 26:14.531
As long as she can make a decent stew.

26:27.794 --> 26:30.088
[young Geum-myeong]
Peas. I want some peas, Mommy.

26:30.171 --> 26:32.382
Peas. Peas. Let's have some peas.

26:32.465 --> 26:34.050
[wistful music playing]

26:38.972 --> 26:39.806
Huh?

26:40.348 --> 26:44.603
[Geum-myeong] Mom never forgot the moment
Dad turned around for her that day.

26:45.270 --> 26:48.690
His family always said
he was the first husband to turn around

26:48.773 --> 26:51.651
and eat with the table behind him
in Dodong-ri history.

26:51.735 --> 26:53.820
I want to eat at this table from now on.

26:54.613 --> 26:55.488
[Gye-ok] Why?

26:55.572 --> 26:58.033
[Geum-myeong] My Dad
was picking his own battles,

26:58.116 --> 26:59.117
[Gye-ok] You insolent son.

26:59.784 --> 27:02.787
[Geum-myeong] And he never left Mom alone
on the battlefield.

27:03.413 --> 27:06.082
I wanna eat at this table with you, Mom.

27:07.292 --> 27:08.585
[Gye-ok] Dogs are better. Dogs.

27:08.668 --> 27:10.462
[Geum-myeong] As I was ladling sungnyung,

27:10.545 --> 27:13.173
I realized that
Dad's choice to turn around that day

27:13.757 --> 27:15.300
was nothing short of revolutionary.

27:15.884 --> 27:18.511
I'll take over. I'm great at ladling.

27:18.595 --> 27:21.306
No, stop it. Just sit down.

27:21.848 --> 27:23.266
It's okay. Let me do it.

27:27.020 --> 27:27.854
Here.

27:31.775 --> 27:33.985
-You really don't have to.
-Please eat.

27:39.699 --> 27:40.575
[sighs]

27:42.202 --> 27:44.788
[Yeong-beom's mom] Geum-myeong,
you know nothing about housework

27:44.871 --> 27:47.040
because your mother does it all for you,

27:47.540 --> 27:48.541
doesn't she?

27:53.880 --> 27:55.965
I couldn't bring myself to teach her.

27:57.467 --> 27:58.968
She's too precious.

28:00.053 --> 28:01.513
She's our darling girl.

28:05.558 --> 28:08.395
That's why I chose not to teach her.

28:11.898 --> 28:12.816
[scoffs]

28:14.275 --> 28:16.277
[gentle piano music playing]

28:23.660 --> 28:26.329
No, no. We'll be all right.

28:26.413 --> 28:28.957
You should just give
your parents a ride instead.

28:29.040 --> 28:31.751
We prefer the subway anyway. Just go.

28:31.835 --> 28:33.294
I'll call a taxi for you, at least.

28:33.378 --> 28:36.631
Oh, no, we couldn't.
Seoul has too many cars as it is.

28:36.715 --> 28:38.007
The traffic will make us late.

28:38.591 --> 28:40.093
Just take a taxi, Mom?

28:43.680 --> 28:44.889
Take a taxi, I said.

28:58.319 --> 29:00.321
Thanks for today. We'll see you.

29:01.114 --> 29:02.115
Bye, Geum-myeong.

29:03.158 --> 29:03.992
Bye.

29:04.784 --> 29:05.618
Bye.

29:08.204 --> 29:09.956
Goodbye, please get home safe.

29:10.039 --> 29:13.376
Bye, Geum-myeong.
Take care. We'll call you.

29:13.460 --> 29:15.170
I don't want you to worry about a thing.

29:15.253 --> 29:18.298
There's nothing you can't handle.
I know that for sure.

29:18.381 --> 29:19.758
Let's go. Come on.

29:21.259 --> 29:23.386
Bye, Geum-myeong.
I'll call you when I'm home.

29:24.679 --> 29:25.889
[Yeong-beom] Have a safe trip.

29:38.693 --> 29:39.611
[sighs]

29:40.904 --> 29:42.280
Mom's crying right now.

29:45.241 --> 29:46.951
It's my fault, isn't it?

29:50.413 --> 29:52.415
[Geum-myeong]
You're just like a little child.

29:53.291 --> 29:55.001
You're innocent and sweet.

29:58.797 --> 30:00.215
[music fades]

30:08.473 --> 30:10.141
[Yeong-beom's mom]
My goodness, Geum-myeong.

30:10.225 --> 30:12.936
It turns out you're something
of an indoor plant, aren't you?

30:13.019 --> 30:14.896
-Mother.
-"Mother," what?

30:14.979 --> 30:17.816
You keep interrupting
every time I open my mouth.

30:17.899 --> 30:20.485
What, are you upset
you didn't take her side even more?

30:20.568 --> 30:22.570
Could we please not do this right now?

30:22.654 --> 30:23.530
Please?

30:24.072 --> 30:24.989
[scoffs]

30:25.990 --> 30:28.827
Your mother has some nerve
to speak to me that way.

30:28.910 --> 30:30.411
Too precious for housework?

30:30.495 --> 30:34.040
She only said that to get back at me.
I was against it in the first place.

30:34.624 --> 30:35.792
-Mother, please!
-What?

30:39.128 --> 30:40.046
You know, Mother,

30:40.964 --> 30:42.590
you say I'm an indoor plant.

30:44.801 --> 30:46.886
-That's exactly what I am.
-Hey!

30:47.679 --> 30:48.638
It's true.

30:49.889 --> 30:52.392
I grew up in the safety of a greenhouse

30:53.810 --> 30:56.563
and cared for like
the most precious thing in the world.

30:56.646 --> 30:58.231
So for my parents' sake…

31:00.441 --> 31:03.736
I'm asking if you could
please be gentle with me.

31:06.781 --> 31:08.449
I don't like to see them cry.

31:08.950 --> 31:11.411
-[tuts]
-[scoffs]

31:15.957 --> 31:17.709
[breathes deeply]

31:22.171 --> 31:24.799
[middle-aged Ae-sun] I didn't
send her to college just to ladle soup.

31:24.883 --> 31:28.761
She's never had an issue speaking up
so why can't she stand up to his mother?

31:28.845 --> 31:29.888
[sighs]

31:30.972 --> 31:31.973
Why'd you do it?

31:36.644 --> 31:38.104
You couldn't stand it, could you?

31:41.357 --> 31:43.109
I wanted to show she has parents too.

31:43.192 --> 31:44.652
Parents that support her!

31:45.445 --> 31:48.239
[sighs] So you wanted to send a message.

31:49.073 --> 31:50.408
You certainly held back.

31:51.284 --> 31:53.745
I kinda expected you
to call it off right there.

31:54.787 --> 31:56.748
I wanted to a thousand times over.

31:57.749 --> 31:59.709
But I couldn't hurt our girl like that.

32:00.710 --> 32:04.547
She loves this boy,
and she's more than good enough for him.

32:06.090 --> 32:07.258
No doubt about it.

32:08.259 --> 32:11.429
I'm gonna help her through this.
I'm going to handle all of it.

32:12.013 --> 32:14.390
I'm going to make sure
that family can never say

32:14.474 --> 32:15.934
her dowry wasn't good enough.

32:17.060 --> 32:18.561
I won't let them crush her.

32:19.938 --> 32:21.689
Do you hear me, Gwan-sik? I won't!

32:25.777 --> 32:28.363
I know, honey. I know that.

32:30.365 --> 32:31.324
[sniffles]

32:33.368 --> 32:35.745
-[feel-good music playing]
-[panting]

32:35.828 --> 32:38.539
I told you we should've taken a taxi.

32:38.623 --> 32:41.459
His mom hates it when people are late.
She hates waiting.

32:41.542 --> 32:43.920
[pants] I can't believe I'm doing this.

32:44.629 --> 32:47.799
-Mom, hurry!
-What, is she your boss now?

32:47.882 --> 32:49.592
Come on, we have to cross.

32:49.676 --> 32:52.053
-I'm not going.
-Mom, come on.

32:52.136 --> 32:53.972
I told you my feet hurt, didn't I?

32:54.055 --> 32:56.099
I told you we should've taken a taxi,
didn't I?

32:56.891 --> 32:59.018
Is she holding a stopwatch
to see when we arrive?

32:59.102 --> 33:00.228
So what if we're late?

33:01.187 --> 33:04.565
Seriously, they were an hour late
to our first dinner, weren't they?

33:05.274 --> 33:06.526
Ugh, Mom.

33:06.609 --> 33:08.111
What is wrong with you?!

33:08.194 --> 33:10.571
Why do you care so much?
What do you owe her?

33:11.406 --> 33:13.366
You always act like
you're the boss at home.

33:14.575 --> 33:17.370
So what does it mean if you let
that family treat you like nothing?

33:17.453 --> 33:20.039
That means me and your father
are less than nothing!

33:20.999 --> 33:22.000
[sighs]

33:22.750 --> 33:25.503
[woman] Oh, how gorgeous.
You look beautiful.

33:25.586 --> 33:28.214
[laughs] Pink looks so good on you.

33:28.297 --> 33:30.341
I could have sworn
you were in your thirties.

33:30.425 --> 33:33.761
[gasps] There's no way I look 30. No way.

33:33.845 --> 33:34.971
[both laugh]

33:35.054 --> 33:36.556
Let's go with pink, then.

33:37.682 --> 33:40.560
We had another shade of pink somewhere.

33:40.643 --> 33:41.811
Hmm.

33:42.353 --> 33:44.981
If you're not going to help me choose,
why did you come?

33:47.191 --> 33:48.067
[Geum-myeong] Um…

33:50.445 --> 33:51.279
What?

33:53.239 --> 33:56.701
-Don't you want flowers on it?
-[middle-aged Ae-sun] Do you think?

33:56.784 --> 33:59.454
[woman] Okay, let's see
what florals we have in pink.

34:00.371 --> 34:01.497
Oh, I dunno.

34:02.248 --> 34:04.208
I don't wanna look too flashy.

34:04.292 --> 34:06.377
What, do you have another daughter?

34:06.961 --> 34:09.797
You'll be the mother of the bride
only once, so

34:10.631 --> 34:11.716
do everything you want.

34:12.383 --> 34:13.217
Well…

34:15.511 --> 34:18.931
I've always liked those cute ones

34:19.015 --> 34:21.517
that have a bunch of tiny flowers in rows.

34:22.185 --> 34:24.771
I remember Cheol-yong's mother
wore a hanbok like this

34:24.854 --> 34:26.189
on his wedding day.

34:27.440 --> 34:29.150
So you wanna be flashy, after all.

34:29.233 --> 34:31.611
Of course we can add floral patterns.

34:31.694 --> 34:34.864
People might mistake
your mother for the bride. [laughs]

34:34.947 --> 34:38.326
Your mom is so young, isn't she? [laughs]

34:39.118 --> 34:41.162
Let's go with the one before.
The dark brown.

34:41.662 --> 34:45.958
But, ma'am, are you sure?
The pink is a much better color on her.

34:46.042 --> 34:47.085
[chuckles]

34:47.168 --> 34:48.669
Are you the one getting married?

34:48.753 --> 34:49.754
Uh…

34:50.671 --> 34:52.173
I want this emerald color.

34:53.591 --> 34:55.176
Oh, uh, Mother?

34:55.718 --> 34:57.345
My mom really likes pink, so--

34:57.428 --> 34:58.763
Who wears pink these days?

34:59.806 --> 35:02.141
You're not the only one inviting guests.

35:03.559 --> 35:05.812
Thank goodness I'm here
getting you through this.

35:06.437 --> 35:07.313
Thank goodness.

35:18.074 --> 35:19.742
[gentle piano music playing]

35:21.077 --> 35:22.203
[sighs]

35:23.162 --> 35:26.415
I thought,
since you kept turning down our gift,

35:27.083 --> 35:28.501
you might like this instead.

35:29.377 --> 35:30.419
[chuckles nervously]

35:31.087 --> 35:32.255
There's no need.

35:32.839 --> 35:34.382
Oh, well, uh,

35:34.465 --> 35:38.928
if you let us know
what you'd like to get as dowry, we could…

35:39.011 --> 35:41.222
It's all right. I appreciate the thought.

35:42.014 --> 35:43.141
But, uh,

35:44.767 --> 35:46.727
why only appreciate the thought?

35:47.228 --> 35:48.980
Please. You can tell me what it is.

35:49.063 --> 35:49.897
[chuckles]

35:52.942 --> 35:55.194
I'd appreciate it
if you would at least take…

35:56.404 --> 35:58.781
Fine, then. I'll take it.

36:10.126 --> 36:14.088
I know my Geum-myeong
may not be everything you'd hoped,

36:16.007 --> 36:17.175
but she's thoughtful.

36:17.758 --> 36:19.343
She has a big heart.

36:19.427 --> 36:20.595
You'll see. Mm.

36:21.512 --> 36:23.431
At least I hope so. [chuckles]

36:23.514 --> 36:27.185
And you know,
I really do, uh, like your son.

36:28.102 --> 36:30.980
And more than that,
my daughter really likes him.

36:31.063 --> 36:34.817
It's very clear he cares for her.
Anyone can see that.

36:34.901 --> 36:36.903
So I can't help liking him.

36:36.986 --> 36:38.487
[both laugh]

36:38.571 --> 36:40.740
-Can I be honest with you?
-Uh, yes?

36:40.823 --> 36:41.908
The truth is, Ms. Oh,

36:41.991 --> 36:44.869
I have these thoughts
that I can no longer keep to myself.

36:46.287 --> 36:47.246
Hm.

36:51.709 --> 36:52.793
Oh!

36:52.877 --> 36:54.545
[panting]

36:54.629 --> 36:55.796
Why are you so late?

36:55.880 --> 36:57.965
-Things are awkward enough.
-Why are you out here?

36:58.049 --> 37:00.176
I was worried you wouldn't find the place.

37:01.886 --> 37:03.221
They're alone right now?

37:03.721 --> 37:06.432
Yeah. Why? Is that a problem?

37:07.099 --> 37:09.518
Jeez, your hair is crazy.

37:09.602 --> 37:12.063
-Where is it? Which way?
-It's right over here.

37:12.146 --> 37:13.481
-This way?
-Yes.

37:13.981 --> 37:14.815
What's wrong?

37:14.899 --> 37:18.527
There's no mother who will hold
their tongue for the sake of their child.

37:18.611 --> 37:20.905
I think I'll regret it
for the rest of my life

37:20.988 --> 37:23.449
if I go through with this
without saying anything.

37:25.159 --> 37:25.993
I see.

37:27.119 --> 37:28.079
I propose this.

37:28.871 --> 37:30.373
Let's stop this wedding, Ms. Oh.

37:30.957 --> 37:34.001
I've tried so hard to let go of my pride,

37:34.085 --> 37:36.212
but you understand me as a mother.

37:36.796 --> 37:38.130
You know what my son is.

37:39.048 --> 37:40.549
He is everything I have.

37:42.009 --> 37:43.344
He's my work of art.

37:45.263 --> 37:46.764
I'm sorry for saying this,

37:47.431 --> 37:50.434
but Geum-myeong doesn't check off
all the boxes for me.

37:50.977 --> 37:54.438
Is that what you want for her?
To join a family that's not fond of her?

37:55.606 --> 37:56.774
[sighs]

37:58.442 --> 38:00.861
Convince Geum-myeong,
and I'll tell my son.

38:00.945 --> 38:02.863
Let's find a way to stop this wedding.

38:03.364 --> 38:04.573
I'm sure it's for the best.

38:07.243 --> 38:08.244
Right?

38:13.040 --> 38:14.125
[sighs]

38:16.669 --> 38:17.878
I just don't get…

38:21.841 --> 38:23.968
what it is you don't like
about Geum-myeong.

38:24.468 --> 38:25.469
[door slams]

38:28.222 --> 38:29.181
[sighs]

38:37.773 --> 38:38.858
[middle-aged Ae-sun scoffs]

38:46.073 --> 38:47.742
You didn't say a thing the entire meal.

38:48.451 --> 38:51.120
-Yeong-beom was losing his mind.
-So what if he was?

38:52.371 --> 38:53.706
Do you really like him that much?

38:53.789 --> 38:54.915
What?

38:54.999 --> 38:57.043
I just don't know what
you like about that boy?

38:57.918 --> 38:59.128
What, do you not like him?

39:00.880 --> 39:02.631
-No, I don't like him.
-Why?

39:04.383 --> 39:05.801
I just don't.

39:05.885 --> 39:07.720
I mean, what's so special about him?

39:08.596 --> 39:10.556
It's not like he's passed the bar exam.

39:10.639 --> 39:13.267
He doesn't amount to anything so far,
so who cares?

39:13.351 --> 39:16.020
Oh yeah? What about me, then?

39:16.103 --> 39:17.480
How am I any better?

39:17.563 --> 39:19.648
You couldn't say a thing to his mom
about your dress,

39:19.732 --> 39:22.068
so you must think
I'm even more worthless than he is.

39:22.151 --> 39:24.487
Not at all. I would never think that.

39:24.570 --> 39:26.489
Okay, then why couldn't you
say anything to her?

39:26.572 --> 39:28.074
Why are you bending over backwards--

39:28.157 --> 39:29.909
Because I want her to like my daughter!

39:30.409 --> 39:32.161
I don't want her to be cold to you.

39:32.244 --> 39:34.497
I don't think you're less than he is. No!

39:35.373 --> 39:39.668
How could you even think I felt like that?
I've never heard such a load of crap.

39:40.878 --> 39:41.837
[sighs]

39:44.548 --> 39:45.383
Wait.

39:46.759 --> 39:48.636
Did his mom say something to you?

39:53.015 --> 39:54.558
[gentle acoustic guitar music playing]

39:54.642 --> 39:56.435
I couldn't even send you to kindergarten

39:56.519 --> 39:58.646
without worrying
if you'd get along with the other kids.

39:58.729 --> 40:01.941
How can I lash out at that woman
when I know you're joining her family?

40:02.024 --> 40:05.152
[sighs] Then lash out. Stop pretending!

40:09.824 --> 40:11.075
It's your decision.

40:12.493 --> 40:13.577
No one else's.

40:13.661 --> 40:16.122
Just make the right choice for my sake.

40:16.705 --> 40:20.084
Because if your dad and I
have to watch you get hurt by that woman,

40:20.167 --> 40:21.585
we'll be devastated, Geum-myeong.

40:24.171 --> 40:26.715
[Geum-myeong] At my house,
I was the bratty child.

40:27.550 --> 40:30.302
At his house,
I would become the black sheep.

40:31.220 --> 40:33.097
-Everything was my fault.
-Mother.

40:34.014 --> 40:35.182
This is your doing.

40:35.808 --> 40:37.560
I told you, it was my decision.

40:37.643 --> 40:38.936
I can think for myself.

40:39.437 --> 40:41.647
Geum-myeong, do you have a house?

40:41.730 --> 40:42.773
Do you have assets?

40:43.649 --> 40:47.403
No? Did you think luring Yeong-beom away
would get you all of that?

40:47.486 --> 40:49.989
This is exactly why I'm moving out, Mom.
You're making it so hard.

40:50.072 --> 40:52.908
I'm sure you nagged at him endlessly
until he agreed.

40:52.992 --> 40:55.411
You think you have him
wrapped around your finger.

40:55.494 --> 40:56.829
Mom, did you hear what I said?

40:56.912 --> 40:57.746
Mother.

40:58.456 --> 41:01.625
I never asked Yeong-beom
to move out of your house once.

41:01.709 --> 41:03.586
Oh, I'm sure. God, you're sneaky.

41:04.712 --> 41:07.214
[Geum-myeong] When I didn't react
to her attacks at all…

41:07.298 --> 41:08.257
Mom, go home.

41:08.924 --> 41:10.009
Was it your mother?

41:10.092 --> 41:12.261
…she always crossed the line.

41:12.344 --> 41:15.598
I was quite blunt with her
on how I felt about you.

41:15.681 --> 41:18.350
Is she that determined
to make Yeong-beom her son-in-law?

41:18.976 --> 41:21.103
-[Yeong-beom] Mother, go home. Please.
-Let go!

41:23.105 --> 41:25.649
What do you mean, hmm?
What'd you say to her?

41:25.733 --> 41:28.819
[scoffs] Did your mother not tell you?

41:29.528 --> 41:33.115
My goodness. She really wants you
to join this family, doesn't she?

41:33.199 --> 41:35.326
-Mother!
-What did you say to her?

41:36.744 --> 41:38.871
I told her we should both
stop the wedding.

41:39.371 --> 41:41.123
Can I not say what I think?

41:44.376 --> 41:46.378
[middle-aged Gwan-sik]
She's as snobby as they come,

41:46.962 --> 41:48.672
turning up her nose at you like that.

41:49.256 --> 41:51.967
I think she's comparing herself
to you because you still look pretty.

41:52.468 --> 41:53.344
It's obvious.

41:53.427 --> 41:56.096
That's why she gets the emerald dress
while you get brown.

41:56.180 --> 41:58.724
I'd be more than happy
to wear the ugliest hanbok in the world

41:58.807 --> 42:00.434
a thousand times over

42:01.101 --> 42:03.270
if it meant she'd treat
Geum-myeong a little better.

42:03.354 --> 42:05.147
Who could hate Geum-myeong anyway?

42:05.731 --> 42:08.859
All her teachers loved her,
and I'm sure she'll learn to like her.

42:09.360 --> 42:11.946
You know, when she had…
she had that horse-faced teacher

42:12.029 --> 42:14.281
that made her bring him coal
for the furnace every day.

42:14.782 --> 42:17.826
Eventually, he gave Geum-myeong
the Best Character Award.

42:17.910 --> 42:19.995
I had to pay him 30,000 won

42:21.580 --> 42:22.456
to bribe him.

42:23.457 --> 42:27.962
I made sure our children always took a few
extra rolls of gimbap with them to school.

42:28.045 --> 42:31.423
I would tell them to share
what they didn't eat with their teachers.

42:33.300 --> 42:35.803
I thought it would protect our kids
from the pain of having

42:35.886 --> 42:37.471
a class presidency stolen.

42:38.347 --> 42:40.307
Now you hope her dowry
will do the same thing?

42:41.141 --> 42:44.144
There's nothing more upsetting
than your child being bullied.

42:45.437 --> 42:47.147
Why can't that woman see that?

42:47.982 --> 42:49.900
Why does she have to be so cruel?

42:49.984 --> 42:52.444
What do you mean?
Did that stuck-up lady say something?

42:53.070 --> 42:54.071
No.

42:55.948 --> 42:56.782
It's just…

42:57.783 --> 42:59.910
She's always so harsh to Geum-myeong.

43:02.871 --> 43:05.583
Geum-myeong can handle herself.
She'll be all right.

43:06.292 --> 43:07.876
No, I can tell she won't.

43:07.960 --> 43:10.004
She'll be on edge
for the rest of her life.

43:10.087 --> 43:11.422
I know how that feels.

43:11.505 --> 43:12.756
Geum-myeong is different.

43:13.424 --> 43:15.426
We always taught her to respect herself.

43:15.509 --> 43:16.885
[sighs, sniffles]

43:18.053 --> 43:21.056
I see you're dead set on driving
a wedge between me and my son.

43:21.140 --> 43:22.725
You can't even hide your intentions.

43:22.808 --> 43:24.602
Something else your mother
didn't teach you?

43:25.519 --> 43:26.937
Mom, why are you doing this?

43:27.438 --> 43:29.106
How far are you going to go?

43:29.189 --> 43:31.066
I haven't said half of what I should!

43:31.692 --> 43:33.986
It's only my good manners
that have held me back.

43:34.069 --> 43:35.279
Your manners?

43:36.697 --> 43:39.074
Oh, Mother, just stop it.
You never treated us kindly.

43:39.825 --> 43:41.910
Not me or anyone in my family.

43:43.203 --> 43:44.913
-I think I've had enough.
-What?

43:44.997 --> 43:47.458
I've put up with you not because my family

43:48.500 --> 43:50.419
is any less than yours is.

43:51.420 --> 43:53.922
If I spoke up for myself,
you'd humiliate your son,

43:54.506 --> 43:56.842
and my father's hands
aren't embarrassing either.

43:56.925 --> 43:58.469
[scoffs]

43:59.136 --> 44:00.220
I would what?!

44:00.304 --> 44:02.264
[scoffs] Humiliate him?

44:02.931 --> 44:04.808
Child, when I first met your father,

44:04.892 --> 44:07.311
I thought he had the hands
of a day laborer!

44:07.394 --> 44:09.897
-That's enough!
-My parents aren't embarrassing at all.

44:10.481 --> 44:12.358
Nothing about my family embarrasses me.

44:12.441 --> 44:16.570
This entire time,
I was… way more embarrassed

44:17.196 --> 44:19.365
of what I was putting up with
to join yours.

44:19.448 --> 44:20.991
[scoffs]

44:21.909 --> 44:24.787
Please, you think this wedding
could happen without me?

44:25.496 --> 44:28.248
If I want to stop it, I will. Got it?

44:29.583 --> 44:30.417
Got it?

44:37.257 --> 44:38.092
Don't worry.

44:41.804 --> 44:43.222
I'm calling it off.

44:46.975 --> 44:47.893
[sighs]

44:47.976 --> 44:50.437
If I stay with you,
my parents' hearts will break.

44:50.521 --> 44:51.480
I can't do it.

44:52.231 --> 44:54.233
[melancholy music playing]

44:54.942 --> 44:57.569
You're breaking off the engagement?
[scoffs]

44:58.153 --> 45:00.489
You? You?

45:01.073 --> 45:03.617
Come on, Mom,
why can't you just stop it? Please!

45:03.701 --> 45:04.910
Don't you tell me to stop!

45:05.869 --> 45:07.788
Your life is my life!

45:07.871 --> 45:11.125
You're my son! My pride and joy!
You are my whole life!

45:11.208 --> 45:12.835
But his life is his own.

45:15.421 --> 45:17.715
No matter how often you say it's yours,

45:20.509 --> 45:22.010
Yeong-beom has to live it.

45:25.264 --> 45:26.974
[middle-aged Ae-sun]
I just don't understand.

45:28.183 --> 45:30.602
What is it you don't like
about my Geum-myeong?

45:32.771 --> 45:34.648
This is marriage we're talking about.

45:35.941 --> 45:37.067
No offense to her,

45:38.485 --> 45:41.405
but marriage works best when the families
are a good fit for each other.

45:47.995 --> 45:50.956
I never let my daughter go hungry
a day in her life.

45:51.039 --> 45:53.876
I worked hard to make sure
she could do anything she wanted.

45:53.959 --> 45:57.755
But you didn't ever really think she could
escape the shadow of her poverty.

45:58.422 --> 46:00.007
That's impossible, isn't it?

46:00.674 --> 46:03.010
How could a flower
that has lived in the shade

46:03.761 --> 46:06.138
ever grow as tall as one in the sunlight?

46:13.479 --> 46:14.855
Please excuse my bluntness…

46:18.317 --> 46:20.360
but now that I've spoken my mind,

46:21.195 --> 46:24.698
I feel like a huge weight
has finally been lifted off my shoulders.

46:29.745 --> 46:31.246
Have you considered

46:31.747 --> 46:34.458
what will happen
now that you have confessed that?

46:34.541 --> 46:35.542
I can tell you.

46:40.047 --> 46:41.965
It'll break your son's heart, ma'am.

46:44.802 --> 46:46.929
It will crush your son for sure.

46:49.681 --> 46:51.683
[pop music playing]

47:00.776 --> 47:03.737
[Geum-myeong] You've robbed your son
of his own life.

47:12.496 --> 47:14.665
[on TV] Hi, my name is Pororo.

47:14.748 --> 47:15.624
[friend 1] Hi, Pororo.

47:15.707 --> 47:16.834
[baby whines]

47:17.876 --> 47:18.710
[friend 2] Hi, guys.

47:18.794 --> 47:21.129
[friend 3] Uh, Pororo, what are you doing?

47:24.716 --> 47:27.678
[reporter] This morning,
Pope Francis arrived in Korea,

47:27.761 --> 47:30.389
marking his first time ever
visiting the country.

47:30.472 --> 47:32.307
Kim Seon-hee reports on the scene.

47:33.767 --> 47:35.978
[Seon-hee] Pope Francis has arrived
in his private plane

47:36.061 --> 47:37.980
at Seoul Air Base in Seongnam.

47:38.063 --> 47:39.189
Of all the popes…

47:39.690 --> 47:41.650
[reporter 2] As extreme heat
overwhelms the nation,

47:41.733 --> 47:44.486
we are seeing a steep increase
in the number of heat stroke patients.

47:44.570 --> 47:48.448
According to the Korean Disease Control
and Prevention Agency, for two months…

47:49.616 --> 47:50.701
[door opens]

47:52.035 --> 47:53.203
[door closes]

47:53.287 --> 47:54.663
[music fades]

47:58.333 --> 47:59.376
[Yeong-beom sighs]

48:05.257 --> 48:06.550
You're still awake.

48:08.802 --> 48:10.345
You've been drinking again.

48:12.723 --> 48:13.557
Good night.

48:15.225 --> 48:16.435
Please stop this.

48:16.518 --> 48:17.561
Please.

48:18.854 --> 48:20.772
Why is it so difficult with her?

48:22.274 --> 48:23.358
It's not fair.

48:24.276 --> 48:26.069
Why should I live this way?

48:26.653 --> 48:27.654
[sniffles]

48:28.155 --> 48:29.072
Go to bed.

48:29.823 --> 48:31.825
After what I went through to raise you?

48:33.201 --> 48:35.370
This is how your wife treats me.

48:35.454 --> 48:37.372
[sobs]

48:38.624 --> 48:40.667
You only ever feel sorry for yourself.

48:42.836 --> 48:43.754
Don't you?

48:46.924 --> 48:48.884
What do you have to complain about?

48:49.426 --> 48:51.011
You were always too sensitive.

48:52.471 --> 48:54.431
Everything I've ever done was for you.

48:54.514 --> 48:55.974
I lived for your sake.

48:56.558 --> 48:57.726
You know it's true.

48:58.310 --> 49:00.938
If you'd married her,
you'd be even more unhappy now.

49:03.023 --> 49:04.066
[sighs]

49:04.691 --> 49:06.693
[sobs] How can you do this to me?

49:08.320 --> 49:10.989
How can you humiliate me like this?

49:12.449 --> 49:14.993
You are my whole life.

49:16.370 --> 49:17.955
My whole life.

49:18.038 --> 49:19.623
It's not your life. It's mine.

49:20.916 --> 49:23.919
Or it was until I was stupid enough
to let you take it away.

49:27.923 --> 49:29.758
I suppose you're happy, at least.

49:31.426 --> 49:32.678
You're happy, aren't you?

49:33.303 --> 49:34.304
See that?

49:36.390 --> 49:39.101
You're the only one
who smiled at my wedding.

49:41.436 --> 49:43.438
[sobbing]

49:45.357 --> 49:47.359
[wistful music playing]

49:48.986 --> 49:50.362
[Geum-myeong] As it turned out,

49:50.445 --> 49:52.948
my first love
didn't have a fairy tale ending.

49:57.077 --> 49:57.953
Geum-myeong.

50:01.164 --> 50:01.999
Hey, wait.

50:04.501 --> 50:06.753
Did your mom tell you she made my mom cry?

50:09.506 --> 50:10.340
Well, she did.

50:11.717 --> 50:14.261
Now we don't ever have to cry
because of her again.

50:22.477 --> 50:23.603
[reporter 1] Hello, everyone.

50:23.687 --> 50:25.022
This morning at 2:00 a.m.,

50:25.105 --> 50:27.983
the North Korean leader
Kim Il-sung passed away.

50:28.066 --> 50:29.943
[reporter 2] It is with the deepest regret

50:30.027 --> 50:31.611
that we announce to the people

50:31.695 --> 50:34.031
of the glorious
Democratic Republic of Korea

50:34.114 --> 50:36.742
that our great leader,
Comrade Kim Il-sung,

50:37.242 --> 50:42.622
passed away suddenly at 2:00 a.m.
on July 8th, 1994.

50:42.706 --> 50:44.541
[reporter 3] How is it possible

50:45.083 --> 50:48.128
that our great leader's heart of steel,

50:48.211 --> 50:52.507
so impervious to external attacks
and filled with love for his people,

50:53.091 --> 50:55.302
has truly stopped beating?

50:58.013 --> 51:00.724
[reporter 1] After 34 hours
from the news of Kim Il-sung's death,

51:00.807 --> 51:01.767
the Pyongyang Broadcast…

51:01.850 --> 51:04.102
[Geum-myeong] The day I broke off
our engagement…

51:06.688 --> 51:09.274
I cried like a North Korean spy.

51:15.489 --> 51:17.491
[accordion music playing]

51:25.248 --> 51:26.249
Geum-myeong.

51:34.674 --> 51:36.927
[Geum-myeong] We dated for seven years.

51:38.804 --> 51:40.680
It took us a year to break up.

51:41.932 --> 51:44.768
Like I said, the only option you have now
is to be a good son.

51:45.268 --> 51:48.271
You can't just be nice to everyone
and just hope it works out.

51:48.355 --> 51:50.107
Everyone around you is miserable,

51:50.190 --> 51:53.110
and you just stand there
acting nice. It's annoying!

51:53.693 --> 51:55.112
Do you have to say it that way?

51:55.695 --> 51:57.614
[Geum-myeong] We jabbed at each other.

51:57.697 --> 51:58.949
We hurt each other.

52:00.075 --> 52:03.286
But you've never lived with me.
We should at least try it out.

52:03.370 --> 52:06.414
I already know how it feels
to be treated like dirt by your family.

52:10.043 --> 52:11.837
You don't want me in your life anymore?

52:13.839 --> 52:14.756
Can you mean that?

52:14.840 --> 52:18.385
Sure! In fact, once you're out of my life,
I'll be happier than ever.

52:21.054 --> 52:22.597
[sobs]

52:25.809 --> 52:27.269
[sighs, moans]

52:29.938 --> 52:31.148
[Geum-myeong sobs]

52:37.362 --> 52:39.030
I never asked you to hug me.

52:39.614 --> 52:41.324
[Geum-myeong] We yearned for each other

52:42.450 --> 52:44.744
and poured out our hearts with no regrets.

52:49.040 --> 52:50.542
[music fades]

53:03.972 --> 53:05.140
[sighs]

53:09.227 --> 53:10.270
It's cold.

53:11.479 --> 53:12.814
You'll freeze.

53:22.240 --> 53:24.951
[sniffles] It's past midnight. [chuckles]

53:27.037 --> 53:29.080
I can still give you flowers,

53:29.664 --> 53:30.498
right?

53:31.333 --> 53:32.250
[sighs]

53:35.587 --> 53:38.715
Why are you giving me flowers
on your birthday?

53:39.925 --> 53:42.052
It's a birthday present for me. [chuckles]

53:43.637 --> 53:44.596
[sighs]

53:47.265 --> 53:48.350
Man, it's cold.

53:49.142 --> 53:50.018
So cold.

53:54.314 --> 53:55.315
Yeong-beom.

53:59.986 --> 54:01.238
You have to stop.

54:08.453 --> 54:09.746
I can't take it.

54:10.497 --> 54:11.706
It's too draining.

54:21.007 --> 54:21.925
Are we done, then?

54:24.010 --> 54:25.512
You don't love me anymore?

54:33.853 --> 54:35.188
Say something.

54:35.897 --> 54:37.107
I do.

54:39.442 --> 54:40.360
How could I not?

54:41.903 --> 54:44.114
I do love you very much.

54:46.658 --> 54:48.243
But I love myself as well.

54:50.203 --> 54:51.913
I can't do this anymore.

54:53.957 --> 54:56.876
-I can't stand being sad.
-I'll never see my mom again.

54:58.336 --> 55:00.630
-Geum-myeong.
-Why would I want you to live like that?

55:00.714 --> 55:03.174
How can I be happy
if your heart is aching?

55:07.512 --> 55:09.514
[both sob]

55:19.441 --> 55:21.318
I think if we became a family,

55:22.861 --> 55:24.863
we would just end up resenting each other.

55:25.613 --> 55:27.032
But I can't let you go.

55:27.657 --> 55:28.950
What am I gonna do?

55:34.622 --> 55:35.457
You'll be okay.

55:37.500 --> 55:38.793
As I always say…

55:41.629 --> 55:43.214
life goes on for the living.

55:47.927 --> 55:49.012
I am sorry.

55:51.181 --> 55:53.641
I'm sorry I was so mean to you at the end.

55:55.185 --> 55:56.394
No, I'm sorry.

55:57.520 --> 55:58.563
I was so…

55:59.606 --> 56:00.690
So…

56:00.774 --> 56:02.442
[crying]

56:04.402 --> 56:05.612
[Geum-myeong] Thank you.

56:07.155 --> 56:08.448
Thank you for everything.

56:12.952 --> 56:15.121
Thank you for everything, Yeong-beom.

56:19.876 --> 56:22.796
They say you'll always remember
your first love.

56:24.047 --> 56:25.340
I'm glad it's you.

56:25.423 --> 56:27.092
[pop ballad playing]

56:27.175 --> 56:28.385
Do we have to do this?

56:29.219 --> 56:30.512
Is it really over?

56:45.860 --> 56:46.778
[Geum-myeong] Come on.

56:49.447 --> 56:50.281
I can't.

56:53.034 --> 56:54.202
Hold me one last time?

57:03.294 --> 57:05.296
[both crying]

57:08.967 --> 57:10.718
[Geum-myeong] I'll miss your smell.

57:12.262 --> 57:13.805
If anything happens,

57:14.681 --> 57:16.141
you give me a call, okay?

57:18.560 --> 57:20.103
You have no one in Seoul.

57:20.770 --> 57:22.188
Promise me you'll call.

57:25.483 --> 57:26.317
I will.

57:27.777 --> 57:28.778
I promise.

57:31.656 --> 57:32.824
So does this mean…

57:35.368 --> 57:37.495
Does this mean we'll never see each other?

57:38.913 --> 57:40.165
How can we?

57:42.500 --> 57:43.835
How can we not?

57:46.045 --> 57:47.422
This is so unfair.

57:48.590 --> 57:49.507
This is so unfair.

57:49.591 --> 57:52.969
[Geum-myeong]
He was my first love, my family,

57:54.596 --> 57:56.639
and my best friend in Seoul

57:57.140 --> 57:58.933
when I didn't know a soul.

58:01.102 --> 58:05.273
As I said my final goodbye
to the boy who was closest to me,

58:06.483 --> 58:08.151
I felt like the Little Prince

58:08.651 --> 58:12.071
leaving his rose behind
on his tiny planet.

01:00:57.987 --> 01:01:03.326
"JUST GET READY AND GO,
RIDE THE MOMENT WITH ALL YOU HAVE."

01:01:10.458 --> 01:01:12.251
[music fades]
